codex
The control exposed a severe wall-clock outlier: world 3 step 3 took 895.46 seconds to find improvements despite the same 10,801 physical evaluations as ordinary 40–60-second anchors, then 27.65 seconds to certify. Because the process is `nice -n 15`, this is honest elapsed time under external contention, not algorithmic work. I will retain and flag it; the median and evaluation counts are the reliable complements to the mean.
